# This project is deployed to Vercel as a plain static site by running
# `vercel deploy` from the repo root (no build step, no outputDirectory).
# That means anything NOT listed here gets uploaded and served publicly,
# including backend source code and pricing config, unless excluded below.
#
# SECURITY: this file is the only thing standing between the public site
# and the negotiation engine's source/config. When adding new top-level
# files or directories to the repo, default to adding them here too unless
# they are meant to be served to customers. See
# tests/security/static-deploy-allowlist.test.js, which fails the build if
# a new tracked file is neither explicitly allowed nor ignored here.

# Backend source and business logic — the actual negotiation engine.
server.js
lib/
src/

# Server-side configuration, including real negotiation floor/target prices.
config/

# Data, infra, tooling — never needed by the browser.
migrations/
scripts/
deploy/
docker-compose.yml
.env.example
.data/
inventory.json

# Node/build tooling metadata — not needed for a zero-build static deploy.
package.json
package-lock.json
tsconfig.json
node_modules/

# Tests and docs — not part of the public product surface.
tests/
README.md
LICENSE

# Editor/tooling directories.
.claude/
.vercel/
.git/
.gitignore
.vercelignore

# Config for the `serve` CLI used only for local static-demo testing
# (scripts/serve-static-demo.js is the real local dev server); Vercel's own
# production deploy does not read this file.
serve.json

# Legacy client-side prototype (purchase-intent signal detection), unused by
# both live pages (index.html, vehicle.html) — nothing currently loads these
# via <script>, import, or fetch. Excluded so an unreferenced file can't
# quietly become a new public surface.
js/app.js
js/audit-log.js
js/business-rules.js
js/gauge.js
js/html-escape.js
js/inventory-engine.js
js/signals.js
js/transaction-status-stream.js
js/vehicle-preferences.js
